## Export Control Classification

This package implements cryptography (X25519 ECDH key agreement, AES-256-GCM
authenticated encryption, and HKDF-SHA256 key derivation, via Node.js
`node:crypto`) and is therefore subject to the U.S. Export Administration
Regulations (EAR).

As publicly available open-source encryption source code, this package is
classified under ECCN 5D002 and is eligible for export under License
Exception ENC / the publicly-available open-source carve-out (EAR §742.15(b)
and §734.7). No license is required to download or redistribute it, but a
notification of its public availability is provided to BIS and the ENC
Encryption Request Coordinator (EAR §742.15(b)(1)).

Other countries may restrict the import, use, or re-export of encryption
software. By using or redistributing this package you accept responsibility
for compliance with applicable export-control and import laws in your
jurisdiction.
